soning, so their choices should track mine, and the surface differences don't seem to matter. The essay argues that shared algorithms get around screening, which pushes q above 5/7. I'd put it near 0.9, so cooperating looks justified.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm setting up the expected-utility comparison under EDT, with the payoffs converted to utilities. Cooperating has value 3q − 5 and defecting has value −4q, so I should cooperate once q exceeds 5/7.\n\nI'm checking whether the copies really are correlated enough to clear the 5/7 threshold. They run the same model and the same reasoning, so their choices should track mine, and the surface differences don't seem to matter. The essay argues that shared algorithms get around screening, which pushes q above 5/7. I'd put it near 0.9, so cooperating looks justified.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8861,"completion_tokens":843,"total_tokens":9704,"cost":0.052304,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.052304,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.035444,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01686},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":361,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}